The MIT licence above covers the NovaSky source code only.

The astronomical catalogues and imagery bundled in resources/ are the work of
others and keep their own licences and attribution requirements. They are
listed in full, with their sources, in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md. In summary:

  HYG database v4.1 (stars)                     CC BY-SA 4.0
  OpenNGC (deep-sky objects)                    CC BY-SA 4.0
  d3-celestial (constellation figures)          BSD-3-Clause
  moment-timezone (time-zone reference points)  MIT
  ESO/S. Brunier, GigaGalaxy Zoom all-sky
    panorama (resources/data/milkyway.jpg)      CC BY 4.0

Data fetched at runtime is not redistributed with this software:

  CelesTrak (satellite orbital elements)
  CDS/Aladin hips2fits and NASA SkyView (DSS survey cutouts), which serve
    imagery from the Digitized Sky Survey; see the DSS copyright notice at
    https://archive.stsci.edu/dss/copyright.html
